<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 9.21 pct, M2 up 3.42 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 9.21 pct, M2 up 3.42 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 894.1 billion levs on June 20 from 818.7 billion levs a week earlier and M2 increased to 3,754.4 billion levs from 3,630.2 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 2.98 percent to 3,971.2 billion levs in the week to June 30.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixings of 1,697.3 levs per dollar on June 20, 1,677.3 for June 13 and 1,568.1 for May 30.</p>
